SimpleComplex <pre><code>{
    "type": "neo-apoli:reference",
    "value": "example:entity/set_on_fire_for_5_secs"//(1)!
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li> <p>The location of the file is <code>data/example/neo-apoli/action/entity/set_on_fire_for_5_secs.json</code> with this as its contents:</p> <pre><code>{
    "type": "neo-apoli:set_entity_on_fire",
    "ticks": 200,
    "entity": "this"
}
</code></pre> </li> </ol> <p>This example invokes the <code>example:entity/set_on_fire_for_5_secs</code> action.</p> <pre><code>{
    "type": "neo-apoli:reference",
    "value": "example:entity/add_local_velocity"/*(1)!*/,
    "parameters": {
        "example:entity_to_launch": {
            "type": "neo-apoli:entity",
            "entity": "this"
        },
        "example:velocity": {
            "type": "neo-apoli:vec3",
            "value": [
                0.0,
                4.0,
                0.0
            ]
        }
    }
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li> <p>The location of the file is <code>data/example/neo-apoli/action/entity/add_local_velocity.json</code> with this as its contents:</p> <pre><code>{
    "type": "neo-apoli:add_velocity",
    "method": "single",
    "space": "local",
    "entity": "example:entity_to_launch",
    "velocity": {
        "type": "neo-apoli:context",
        "parameter": "example:velocity"
    }
}
</code></pre> </li> </ol> <p>This example provides the context parameters (specifically used by the action) before invoking the <code>example:entity/add_local_velocity</code> action.</p>

FullInlined <pre><code>{
    "type": "neo-apoli:sequence",
    "actions": [
        {
            "type": "neo-apoli:set_entity_on_fire",
            "ticks": 80,
            "entity": "this"
        },
        {
            "type": "neo-apoli:add_velocity",
            "method": "single",
            "space": "world",
            "entity": "this",
            "velocity": [
                0.0,
                4.0,
                0.0
            ]
        }
    ]
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>[
    {
        "type": "neo-apoli:set_entity_on_fire",
        "ticks": 80,
        "entity": "this"
    },
    {
        "type": "neo-apoli:add_velocity",
        "method": "single",
        "space": "world",
        "entity": "this",
        "velocity": [
            0.0,
            4.0,
            0.0
        ]
    }
]
</code></pre> <p>This example will set the entity from the <code>neo-apoli:this_entity</code> context parameter on fire for 4 seconds and launch them up into the sky.</p>

SimpleComplex <pre><code>{
    "type": "neo-apoli:reference",
    "value": "example:entity/is_in_water"//(1)!
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li> <p>The location of the file is <code>data/example/neo-apoli/condition/entity/is_in_water.json</code> with this as its contents:</p> <pre><code>{
    "type": "neo-apoli:compare",
    "comparison": {
        "type": "neo-apoli:float",
        "comparator": "&gt;",
        "first": {
            "type": "neo-apoli:entity/fluid_height",
            "fluid_tag": "#minecraft:water",
            "entity": "this"
        },
        "second": 0.0
    }
}
</code></pre> </li> </ol> <p>This example invokes the <code>example:entity/is_in_water</code> condition and returns its result.</p> <pre><code>{
    "type": "neo-apoli:reference",
    "value": "example:item/is_armor_higher_than_threshold"/*(1)!*/,
    "parameters": {
        "example:item": {
            "type": "neo-apoli:item",
            "value": "worn_item"
        },
        "example:threshold": {
            "type": "neo-apoli:float",
            "value": 2.0
        }
    }
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li> <p>The location of the file is <code>data/example/neo-apoli/condition/item/is_armor_higher_than_threshold.json</code> with this as its contents:</p> <pre><code>{
    "type": "neo-apoli:compare",
    "comparison": {
        "type": "neo-apoli:float",
        "comparator": "&gt;",
        "first": {
            "type": "neo-apoli:item/attribute",
            "attribute": "minecraft:armor",
            "item": "example:item"
        },
        "second": "example:threshold"
    }
}
</code></pre> </li> </ol> <p>This example provides the context parameters (specifically used by the condition) before invoking the <code>example:item/is_armor_higher_than_threshold</code> condition.</p>

